{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And moreover she is indeed my sister, etc.</b> Here Abraham was obligated to Abimelech and extricated himself also from the complaint that Abimelech raised against him, having confronted him with ״What have you done to us?״ etc. And he said <b>And moreover she is indeed my sister</b> etc. — now, did I say she is not my wife in order to provoke you, that I misled God-fearers? I said 'my sister,' and she can be both my sister and my wife, and it is upon you to ask whether she is my wife even though I said 'my sister,' for I am permitted to call her my sister, and this does not constitute a declaration that she is not my wife to anyone who fears and trembles from sinning before Elohim. And perhaps it was on account of this argument that Abimelech sensed that truth was with Abraham, and he gave him good gifts. He also intended this so they would not suspect him of uttering a falsehood from his mouth, for the righteous are scrupulous about deception and anything resembling it."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:31.435049264Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}